# Trivy config (Terraform IaC) baseline — ADR-046.
#
# Contract: explicit, dated and reviewable. Each entry carries
# `# expiry: YYYY-MM-DD` on the line above it or inline, and CI fails once
# past that date. Do NOT use trivy's own `expiredAt:` field — 0.71.0 accepts
# it and does not honour it (measured; see ADR-046).
#
# The gate runs at --severity CRITICAL,HIGH,MEDIUM,LOW as of 2026-09-05.
#
# KNOWN LIMITATION, stated rather than hidden: the plain ignore format
# suppresses a check id REPO-WIDE, not per resource. Every entry below is
# justified for LOG-SINK buckets only, and a suppression of that shape would
# also silence the same finding on a bucket that is not a log sink. The
# compensating discipline is the review question attached to each entry —
# verify WHICH buckets the check currently fires on, not just that the
# justification still reads well. Trivy's YAML format supports `paths:`
# scoping and would be tighter; it is not used because its sibling field
# `expiredAt:` is silently ignored, and one parser over one format is worth
# more here than per-path precision on a four-entry file.

# --- Access-log sinks: object versioning ------------------------------------
#
# Fires on the GCP access-logs bucket, the AWS access-logs bucket, and the
# AWS bootstrap tfstate access-log bucket. All three are append-only,
# write-once, never mutated in place, and bounded by a lifecycle rule.
# Versioning protects against overwrite and modification of EXISTING objects
# — not a failure mode for an append-only sink — and multiplies storage cost
# on the highest-volume buckets in the project.
#
# Accepted risk, not a tool limitation: the check is correct in general and
# does not apply to this object lifecycle. The buckets holding state, models
# and MLflow artifacts DO have versioning, and that is where it matters.
#
# Review question: are all three still access-log-only? If any starts holding
# something mutable, this acceptance is void.
# expiry: 2027-03-05  reason: ADR-046 — append-only log sinks, versioning is not a control here
GCP-0078
# expiry: 2027-03-05  reason: ADR-046 — append-only log sinks, versioning is not a control here
AWS-0090

# --- Access-log sinks: logging the log bucket -------------------------------
#
# Fires on the AWS bootstrap tfstate access-log bucket, which does not log its
# own access. Enabling that requires a third bucket, which would then require
# a fourth: the regress has no fixed point, and AWS rejects self-logging.
#
# The bucket it protects — the Terraform state bucket — IS logged, which was
# the point of adding it (2026-09-05 LOW triage). Note that adding it to close
# one LOW finding introduced three new ones, one of them HIGH; two were fixed
# (CMK encryption, public-access block) and this is the residue.
#
# Review question: is the STATE bucket still logged? That is the control this
# entry must not be allowed to hide.
# expiry: 2027-03-05  reason: ADR-046 — log-sink self-logging has no fixed point; the bucket it protects is logged
AWS-0089
